---
title: Filled Chocolate Cupcakes
author: Mary Arntson
category: Desserts
cook time: 20-25 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@flour{2.5%cups}
@sugar{2%cups}
@baking powder{1%tsp}
@salt{1/4%tsp}
@vanilla{1%tsp}
@cocoa{0.5%cup}
@eggs{2}
@salad oil{1%cup}
@buttermilk{1%cup}
@hot water{1%cup} (with 2 tsp baking soda dissolved in it)
@sugar{0.5%cup}
@milk{1/3%cup}
@shortening{1%cup}
@salt{1/4%tsp}
@water{1%Tbsp}
@powdered sugar{0.5%cup}
@flavoring as desired

Mix all ingredients (except hot water mixture) and beat well. Add 1 c hot water with 2 tsp baking soda dissolved in it. Bake in cupcake cups for 20-25 minutes at 350 degrees.

**Filling:**
Combine sugar, milk, shortening, salt, water and flavoring. Beat 5-7 minutes. Add 1/2 cup powdered sugar and beat 5 minutes more. Fill cooled cupcakes with filling through the top of the cupcake using a cake decorator. Frost.
